    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144-a1">

                <pb facs="0325" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg197"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Francisco, Cal.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-06T21:04:00-08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi>
                            6, 1885—9.04 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cheng</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chinese Legation, Washington, D. C.:</hi></p>
                <p>Telegrams this clay from Washington Territory show that outrages are still going.
                    Last night all Chinese driven from Puyallup, and matters hourly getting worse.
                    No troops sent. The Chinese ordered to leave Seattle to-day. Strong appeals for
                    protection received here hourly. The mayor of Seattle asked governor for troops
                    on the 4th, but refused.</p>
                <closer><signed>OWYANG MING.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
